From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: djvalic <djvalic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ad5x: About's Processor value translated
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The previous patch's Processor row built its value in English inside
kiln_hardware, so a Russian screen showed "Процессор" next to "variant
unknown". kiln_hardware now only reads and decodes, as for the eMMC:
read_processor() returns the eFuse's SocInfo (variant, DDR3, RAM size,
SoC ID), the boot loader's ad5x.ram= size when there is no eFuse, and
the core revision. The About panel reads it once and turns it into text
in populate_info_rows() with lv_tr() and the English format strings as
keys, so the row follows the language each time About opens. Chip
names, DDR2/DDR3 and "SoC ID" stay untranslated. The keys are in en.yml
and, with Russian values, in ru.yml; other languages show English.

Also:
- a variant code of 7 or more (Ingenic lists 0-6, U-Boot's
  X2600_SOC_KNOWN) shows "X2600, variant unknown (N)", not
  "X2600 variant N"
- the nvmem device scan uses directory_iterator's non-throwing
  increment; it runs on the UI thread
- the processor value buffer is 160 bytes: Russian text is longer
  than 96
- kiln_hardware.h notes that the ad5x.ram= rule is bl_variant's
  (lib/bootloader.sh), not mem_hw_mib's last-wins, and that the eFuse
  cell is root-only (kernel patch 0085), so the row falls back if
  HelixScreen stops running as root
- kiln_hardware.cpp no longer includes fmt: nothing there formats now

The tests check the fields: unknown variant codes, a cell on the second
nvmem device, a cell that can't be read (falls back to ad5x.ram=) and
no cpuinfo.
